WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.002 --> 00:00:06.452
This is pi-account-guard. Rotate accounts freely, and never send a turn into the wrong zone.

2
00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:26.178
Many of us use a work account and a personal account in the same pi. Here, pi is open in my dotfiles, a personal repository, but the selected model is GPT-5.5, on the company's OpenAI key. The footer already warns about it.

3
00:00:26.782 --> 00:00:29.957
Let's ask what install dot sh does.

4
00:00:30.692 --> 00:00:53.342
Before anything is sent, pi-account-guard checks the account against this place. An account is a provider plus where its key comes from, here the OPENAI underscore API underscore KEY variable. That account is tagged work, and this repository is personal. So the turn is blocked, and nothing reaches the company's OpenAI account.

5
00:00:53.950 --> 00:01:01.375
The fix is one keystroke away. The first choice switches to Claude Sonnet, on my personal Anthropic key.

6
00:01:02.594 --> 00:01:07.244
The same prompt runs again on Claude, and the footer shows a match.

7
00:01:07.846 --> 00:01:16.746
Accounts start untagged. Let's switch to Gemini Flash, on a Google key the guard has never seen, and ask for a git alias.

8
00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:24.809
Before the turn goes, the guard asks which zones this Google account belongs to. Nothing is ticked for you.

9
00:01:25.412 --> 00:01:30.862
We tick personal. The turn goes at once, and the tag is saved for next time.

10
00:01:31.468 --> 00:01:44.968
Rotators and routers switch accounts on their own, sometimes in the middle of a turn. Let's ask for a long review of my zshrc, then switch to GPT-5.5 while it streams.

11
00:01:54.177 --> 00:02:01.152
The guard catches the change and stops the turn at once. It is aborted, not finished on the work account.

12
00:02:01.758 --> 00:02:11.758
Once pi is idle, the account it was on comes first. There is no allow once here, because the aborted turn is gone. We switch back to Gemini.

13
00:02:14.571 --> 00:02:23.521
Finally, slash guard shows what the guard sees. This directory matches no place rule, so it falls to the default zone, personal.

14
00:02:24.126 --> 00:02:29.751
The Google account is tagged personal, so it matches, and turns here go through.

15
00:02:30.356 --> 00:02:37.406
To install it, run the command on screen. Then try slash guard tour, or add your first place rule.
